---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';
const site = siteFromHost();
const path = '/compare/postscript-vs-mailchimp';
const title = "Postscript vs Mailchimp for Shopify: 2026 Comparison";
const desc = "Keep the working email audience or migrate the channel? A Shopify workflow and migration comparison, with current supplier sources.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can Mailchimp receive SMS replies?",
    "answer": "Mailchimp documents SMS conversations in Inbox. Confirm the plan and approved SMS program needed for your account and test your staff\u2019s handling process."
  },
  {
    "question": "Must I replace Mailchimp email when adding Postscript?",
    "answer": "No. Keeping email and adding a text sender is an architecture option, provided you verify ownership, subscription state and purchase suppression across both."
  },
  {
    "question": "At what SMS volume should I migrate?",
    "answer": "There is no evidenced universal threshold. Compare the unmet workflow, eligible markets, contract and usage costs, staffing and migration risk."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a></nav>
      <header class="max-w-4xl"><p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head</p><h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Postscript vs Mailchimp for Shopify</h1><p class="mt-7 text-xl">Keep the working email audience or migrate the channel?</p></header>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>Correct the one-way SMS assumption</h2>
        <p>Mailchimp documents SMS replies in <a href="https://mailchimp.com/help/view-and-manage-inbox-messages/">Mailchimp Inbox</a>. Its <a href="https://mailchimp.com/help/set-up-sms-marketing/">SMS setup guide</a> requires approval of a sending program. The old claim that Mailchimp cannot handle replies is not a sound reason to migrate. Confirm the applicable plan, country and approved program before comparing inbox operation.</p>
        <h2>Audit the connected Shopify audience</h2>
        <p>Mailchimp’s <a href="https://mailchimp.com/help/mailchimp-shopify-syncing/">Shopify syncing guide</a> describes customer events for automation and email/SMS activity syncing back to Shopify. Start by identifying the connected audience and the subscribed states actually present there. Inspect duplicate profiles, archived contacts and old signup forms before adding another sender; a new tool does not repair ambiguous source records.</p>
        <h2>Keep newsletter assets separate from text selection</h2>
        <p>Inventory templates, campaign archives, landing pages, forms and integrations the team uses. If these still serve the business, adding a dedicated text tool need not force immediate email replacement. If email itself needs improvement, define the missing events or segments first. There is no universal deadline after which a merchant must leave Mailchimp.</p>
        <h2>Proposed launch rehearsal for a limited release</h2>
        <p>Create a draft launch for eligible SMS subscribers, with a recent-purchase exclusion and a product link whose destination can sell out. Inspect encoding and message length, required credits or usage allowance, approval status and the operator’s pause procedure. Ask how a shortage or sending failure is reported. This is a proposed rehearsal; we have no evidence that Mailchimp exhausted credits in the merchant stories previously printed here.</p>
        <h2>Try reply handling before rejecting consolidation</h2>
        <p>Use a permitted test contact to ask a shipping question, send an opt-out and return later with another question. Check staff access, assignment, customer context and escalation into the existing support process. Compare that process with the proposed Postscript setup. Neither a feature checkbox nor an invented conversion story proves which inbox your staff can run better.</p>
        <h2>If both tools stay, assign each journey</h2>
        <p>Write a sender map for welcome, cart, post-purchase education and winback. Decide whether email and text complement each other or are mutually exclusive for that journey. Confirm the identity fields and purchase/opt-out updates that reach both systems, including already queued messages. Do not assume a native suppression bridge or invent a custom email-hash integration as an observed implementation.</p>
        <h2>Quote retained assets and new usage together</h2>
        <p>Compare staying with Mailchimp email plus eligible SMS against retaining email and adding Postscript. Include the existing audience bill, SMS usage and country mix, migration labor, inbox staffing and overlapping capture tools. Confirm credit replenishment and billing behavior from the actual proposal. Attributed revenue is not incremental profit, and this page supplies no fixed contact threshold or financial winner.</p>
        <h2>Choose a channel project you can finish</h2>
        <p>Keep Mailchimp if its demonstrated email and text workflows meet the brief; investigate Postscript when a specific unmet text requirement warrants a second platform or migration. If replacing email too, confirm access and workflow coverage separately. Retain templates and subscription evidence until the new sender is validated, and record which automations must be paused at cutover.</p>
        <h2>Postscript scope and evidence limits</h2>
        <p>Postscript describes <a href="https://postscript.io/features">Shopify SMS workflows</a> and has announced <a href="https://postscript.io/email">Postscript Email with a waitlist</a>. Confirm account access before retiring an email sender. Supplier descriptions checked November 25, 2026; no live account tests, performance results or compliance ranking are claimed here.</p>
      </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-mailchimp">Klaviyo vs Mailchimp</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/postscript-vs-brevo">Postscript vs Brevo</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/fashion">Email apps for fashion stores</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Abandoned cart playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Postscript vs Mailchimp FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
